  "description": "Keeps where a sequence's parts go and how far apart: column widths and gaps, rows, lifelines and frames. Each part's own size, a head card's, a message's or a note's plate, an arrow's ends, an activation bar, a self loop, a fragment's head and bounds and the flow's tab, comes from Flow part measures (ADR 0088); its own sheet (design.rs) holds only placement spacing. A fragment's head is measured once where the frame is placed and carried in its rows.",
